  "result": "The node **LVMC_11_52_300** did not pass the gate: the final verdict is `BARE_LITERAL`. I used 1 of the 6 gate runs and stopped, because the problem is in the node's blueprint record, not in the Lean.\n\nI wrote the rule and all five witnesses (forbid, permit, idle, blind, branch_1) in full. They follow the node's mapping, and I declared no narrowing of my own.\n\n**Problem 1: the hours (span s6) can't be written with the literals the node declares.**\n- Civil time only gives the time of day as a count of minutes (`minute_of_day`, e.g. 70 at 01:10).\n- The node declares \"one a.m.\" and \"six a.m.\" in hours, which become 3,600 s and 21,600 s.\n- Comparing the two needs a factor of 60 s per minute. The node doesn't declare that literal, so the gate rejects it.\n- Without the factor the comparison is wrong (70 ≥ 3,600 is false), so the hours would never hold.\n- The only other route is building 60 out of the declared figures by arithmetic, which would be a hidden literal, so I didn't do it.\n- **Fix in the plan:** declare the hours in minutes of day (60 and 360), or declare a 1-minute literal on s6.\n\n**Problem 2: the trailer witnesses can never be violated.**\n- The narratives use \"a trailer, not a motor vehicle\". The run's reading lists `trailer_or_combination` as *unresolved* for the motor-vehicle definition (DEF-NRS-484A-130).\n- That makes a trailer's motor-vehicle status unknown, never false, so the \"except for a motor vehicle\" exception is unknown and `forbid` can't come out violated.\n- The only vehicle classes the reading treats as definitely not motor vehicles are taxicabs, official vehicles and the like. In reality those are motor vehicles, so a scene using one would be false.\n- So with any realistic vehicle the rule can never be violated.\n- **Fix in the plan:** the reading should decide that a trailer that isn't self-propelled is not a motor vehicle, or the scenarios should be re-planned.\n\nWhile working I mistakenly tried to run the gate with an extra `--help`. It was blocked automatically and did not run.\n\n`task_result.md` is in the working directory (`results/full221-1116-1018/iter-002/code/LVMC_11_52_300/`). It has the details and the fixes the plan needs.",
